Dear All,

Can someone please help me with this query about the interpretation of terms in the rem.dyad model in relevent in R?

I am particularly interested in the distinction between this term:

PSAB-BA: P-Shift effect (turn receiving) ? AB->BA (dyadic)

And these two terms:

RRecSnd: Recency of receipt of actions from v? affects v?s future rate of sending to v?
RSndSnd: Recency of sending to v? affects v?s future rate of sending to v?

My guess is the PSAB-BA refers specifically to the very next event that happens and whether this is a reciprocated action, whereas the other two terms RRecSnd and RSndSnd are more general exchanges for recent events, which makes me wonder how exactly "Recency" is defined.

Can someone please give me an example of the difference of their interperpration and/or point me to a relevant reference online or elsewhere?

Thanks a lot!

Cheers,

Mark.

