	<003b01ce3657$6c3c7840$44b568c0$@unm.edu>
Message-ID: <alpine.WNT.1.10.1304102011580.3092@morrism-PC>

You're breaking new ground here, so may need to try different options. 
One thing to remember about the AH data is that *lots* of ties are 
already missing, because of absentee student (affects outdegree) and 
nominations to non-unique nodes (out of school, in sister school, and 
not on roster).

We don't know much about the sensitivity of ERGM estimates to these 
types of missing data.  Missing links for a given number of nodes is one 
thing.  But missing nodes (i.e., non-unique node identifiers) is another.

It's worth keeping in mind that without knowing the true values, 
you'll be unable to distinguish differences in network properties, from 
the differences you're trying to identify with cross-validation.

What is the actual question you're trying to answer?

