of the ergm tutorial examples had similar behavior with the latest update 
of the ergm package.  The example had, in fact, been chosen because it 
displayed near degenerate behavior.  But it used to converge with the seed 
set to 1, and no longer did after the update.  The seed behavior is 
influenced by other dependencies and changes in the code -- it's 
unfortunate but unavoidable.  But the appearance of degeneracy is a 
different issue.  I think that suggests that the model was probably close 
to degenerate in the original case as well.

Dave and/or Pavel, can you comment?

best,
