References: <201308021536210584781@126.com>
Message-ID: <51FBDD4B.2010107@skyeome.net>

Dear ya,

I think it is likely that the as.factor() around the first data element 
is breaking the vertex data import.

For example, this works fine:

test<-network(network.initialize(3),vertex.attr=list(c("A","B","C")),vertex.attrnames=list("Letters"))

but this breaks:

test<-network(network.initialize(3),vertex.attr=list(as.factor(c("A","B","C"))),vertex.attrnames=list("Letters"))

Error in set.vertex.attribute(g, vertex.attrnames[[i]], 
vertex.attr[[i]]) :
   Inappropriate value given in set.vertex.attribute.

If your goal is to convert dutchdata[,46] into numeric values, maybe it 
would work to wrap it in a call to as.numeric:

as.numeric(as.factor(dutchdata[,46]))

best,
  -skye

