I have figured out that I actually do not need to covert the categorical variables to factors because my goal was to fit a ERGM model. When fitting this model, the ergm-terms provide function for recognizing if a variable is categorical or continuous. For instance, if I include a gender predictor, then I can treat gender as continous and put it into the network object, then I fit the ERGM in which the gender is used with "nodefactor" like this: nodefactor(gender). In this way, the gender variable will be treated as a factor.

Thank you very much for the help.

